export const REFUND_EN = "# soluma Refund Policy\n\n**Effective Date**: May 22, 2026\n\n---\n\nThis Policy explains refund standards for paid purchases on the mobile application **\"soluma\"** (operated by ROOT CO., Ltd). It follows Korea's E-Commerce Act and Apple/Google platform refund policies.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Basic Principles\n\n1. All payments are displayed in **US Dollars (USD)** and processed exclusively via **Apple App Store** or **Google Play Store** in-app purchases (IAP).\n2. **Refund requests for in-app purchases must be submitted directly to the platform (Apple/Google)**. The Company processes refunds based on the platform's decision.\n3. Due to digital content's nature, refunds may be limited once content is delivered or use begins.\n4. Korean residents may exercise withdrawal rights under the E-Commerce Act under certain conditions.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Refund Standards by Product Type\n\n### 2.1 Auto-renewing Subscription (Monthly/Yearly)\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Not used after purchase | **Yes** (request via platform) |\n| Partially used | **Limited** (platform policy) |\n| Auto-renewed without use | **Yes** (within reasonable time) |\n| Don't want auto-renewal | **Must cancel directly 24h before expiry** |\n\n**Cancellation**: Cancel directly in your Apple ID or Google account subscription settings. The Company cannot cancel auto-renewal on your behalf.\n\n### 2.2 One-time Purchases (Christ Test, Faith Checkup, Deep Analysis)\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Within 7 days, unused | **Yes** |\n| Used | **Limited** (refundable only if content is defective) |\n\n### 2.3 Bible Lifetime License\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Within 7 days, unused | **Yes** |\n| After 7 days or used | **Limited** |\n\n### 2.4 Credit Top-up\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Unused credit within 7 days | **Yes** (Korean residents, E-Commerce Act) |\n| Used credit | **No** |\n| Bonus credit (promotional) | **No** (free promotional credit) |\n\n**Calculation**: Partial refund of unused credit proportionally, excluding bonus portion.\n\n### 2.5 License Pass\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Used by self | **No** |\n| Unused, within 7 days | **Yes** (Korean residents) |\n| Sent as gift | See Gift Refund |\n| Received from others | **Sender must initiate refund** |\n\n### 2.6 Gifts\n\n| Situation | Refundable? |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| Unused by recipient (within 30 days) | **Yes** (request to Company) |\n| Used by recipient | **No** |\n| Expired after 30 days | **No** (auto-forfeited) |\n\n### 2.7 Talents\n\n- Talents are **non-monetary reward points** and not refundable/convertible.\n\n---\n\n## 3. How to Request Refunds\n\n### 3.1 Apple App Store (iOS)\n1. Visit **reportaproblem.apple.com** or **Settings > [Your Name] > Purchase History**\n2. Or use \"Refund Request\" link in the receipt email\n3. Processed per Apple's policy (typically results within 48 business hours)\n\n### 3.2 Google Play (Android)\n1. Visit **play.google.com/store/account**\n2. Select \"Refund\" on the relevant purchase\n3. Or contact Google Play Support\n4. Within 48 hours of purchase: automatic refund possible\n\n### 3.3 Direct Contact to Company\nFor the following cases, contact us:\n- Platform denied refund despite clear product defect\n- Gift refund/recovery (sender request)\n- Partial refund of unused credit/license (Korean residents)\n\n**Contact**: **master@root2christ.com**\n\n**Submit**:\n- Account email or member ID\n- Receipt number or payment timestamp\n- Refund reason and supporting materials\n\n---\n\n## 4. Processing Time\n\n| Channel | Time |\n|---------|------|\n| Apple App Store | Per Apple policy (typically 48h) |\n| Google Play | Per Google policy (typically 48h) |\n| Company direct | Within **7 business days** |\n\nRefunds are returned via the original payment method. Receipt timing depends on card issuer / platform.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cases Where Refund Is Limited\n\n1. **Account terminated for ToS/legal violation**: No refund\n2. **Fraudulent payment / refund abuse**: Refund denied, future payments restricted\n3. **Promotional free items** (bonus credits, free passes): No refund\n4. **Talents**: No refund\n5. **Long time elapsed**: Platform policies have time limits\n\n---\n\n## 6. Global User Notice\n\n### Korean Residents\n- E-Commerce Act §17: **7-day withdrawal right from payment**\n- However, withdrawal may be restricted if digital content was delivered and use began (Act §17(2))\n\n### U.S. Residents\n- Digital content refunds are generally limited; platform (Apple/Google) policies apply first\n\n### Other Countries\n- Additional rights may apply per resident country consumer protection laws\n\n---\n\n## 7. Dispute Resolution\n\nFor refund disputes:\n\n1. Contact our customer support (**master@root2christ.com**)\n2. Korean residents: **Korea Consumer Agency** (kca.go.kr, 1372)\n3. U.S. residents: Your state's consumer protection agency\n4. Ultimately: Lawsuit per **Terms of Service Article 18**\n\n---\n\n## 8. Policy Changes\n\nThis Policy may change due to legal, platform, or Company policy updates. Changes will be notified in-app at least 7 days before the effective date.\n\n---\n\n**Supplementary Provisions**\n\nThis Refund Policy takes effect on May 22, 2026.\n\nContact: master@root2christ.com\n";
